Based on the provided app name and purpose, here is a detailed multi-screen specification for the QuickBill Pro mobile web app. The app will consist of five files: `index.html`, `style.css`, `db.js`, `components.js`, and `app.js`. Below is the structure and content for each file.

### 1. `index.html`
This file serves as the main entry point for the app, including the splash screen, login, and main app interface.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
    <script src="db.js" defer></script>
    <script src="components.js" defer></script>
    <script src="app.js" defer></script>
    <title>QuickBill Pro</title>
</head>
<body>
    <div id="splash-screen">
        <img src="logo.png" alt="QuickBill Pro Logo" id="logo">
        <p id="version">Version 1.0</p>
    </div>

    <div id="app" class="hidden">
        <div id="profile-drawer" class="drawer">
            <h2>Profile</h2>
            <p id="profile-name"></p>
            <p id="profile-mobile"></p>
            <p id="shop-type"></p>
            <p id="total-bills"></p>
            <p id="total-sales"></p>
            <button id="logout-btn">Logout</button>
        </div>

        <div id="top-bar">
            <h1>QuickBill Pro</h1>
            <div id="live-status">
                <p id="live-sales">Today's Sales: Rs. 0</p>
                <p id="pending-udhar">Pending Udhar: Rs. 0</p>
                <p id="total-bills-display">Total Bills: 0</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <nav id="bottom-nav">
            <button id="tab-home">Home</button>
            <button id="tab-billing">Billing</button>
            <button id="tab-khata">Khata & Notes</button>
            <button id="tab-profile">Profile & History</button>
        </nav>

        <div id="content"></div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
```

